<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="S1a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Supplementary Material</h2>

<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.1 </span>SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details</h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 1: Speech-to-text conversion.</span>
We used WhisperX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, built on Whisper Large v3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, to transcribe audio and generate millisecond-accurate word-level timestamps via forced alignment. This enables reliable video–text pairing for subsequent segmentation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 2: Hierarchical segmentation.</span>
We employed GPT-4o to restructure transcriptions into three hierarchical levels of surgical workflow: phases, steps, and tasks, following the SAGES consensus guidelines <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>. Figure <a href="#S1.F8" title="Fig. 8 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows the prompting template. Word-level timestamps were then used to align captions with clips, producing multi-granular datasets <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{phase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>phase</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{phase}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>step</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{step}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{task}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 3: Dual-model filtering.</span>
At the clip level, we combined visual and textual checks to remove irrelevant or non-descriptive pairs.
For visual filtering, we benchmarked three OpenCLIP models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>(ViT-G/14, ViT-SO400M/14, and ViT-SO400M-14-SigLIP-384) on 159 manually labeled clips (59 surgical, 100 non-surgical). We adopted SigLIP as it achieved the best results. We compared two strategies for clip classification: majority voting over sampled frames vs. mean-pooled frame embeddings. Majority voting yielded more robust results. With 24 frames per clip and a <math id="S1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;50\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;50\%</annotation></semantics></math> voting threshold, we achieved 96.6 F1, 94.29 precision, and 99.0 recall for surgical classification. Figure <a href="#S1.F1a" title="Fig. 1 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows the prompt templates we used for surgical and non-surgical classes and Figure <a href="#S1.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrates examples for both classes.
For textual filtering, we used GPT-4o with a binary decision prompt (Fig. <a href="#S1.F9" title="Fig. 9 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to retain only descriptive captions; examples of descriptive and non-descriptive captions are displayed in Figure <a href="#S1.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. A pair was preserved if it passed both filters and Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> portrays raw count, and the resulting counts after dual-filtering separately and combined.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 4: Contextual Caption Enrichment.</span>
For each clip–caption pair <math id="S1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{g}_{ij},y^{g}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{g}_{ij},y^{g}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>, we utilize <span id="S1.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">GPT-4o</span> using the prompt shown in Figure <a href="#S1.F10" title="Fig. 10 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>
to instruct the model to generate an enriched caption <math id="S1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}^{g}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}^{g}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on a fixed window of <math id="S1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math> preceding captions at the same granularity level, the video title, and the surgical procedure type. Figure <a href="#S1.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ 1.1 SurgLaVi Data Processing Pipeline Details ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>
showcases examples of raw narrations along with their corresponding enhanced version.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1a" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/zero-shot-visual-filtering-prompts.svg" id="S1.F1a.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:191/222;" width="191" height="222"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>Textual prompts for zero-shot classification into <span id="S1.F1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">surgical</span> (green) and <span id="S1.F1a.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-surgical</span> (red) classes using SigLIP. Class embeddings are obtained by averaging multiple prompts.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/filtering_counts.svg" id="S1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/101;" width="191" height="101"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Filtering impact on SurgLaVi<math id="S1.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathbf{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathbf{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and SurgLaVi. Clip–caption pairs are progressively reduced through surgical filtering, descriptiveness filtering, and the intersection of both.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/taxonomy.svg" id="S1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:286/287;" width="286" height="287"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 3: </span><span id="S1.F3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Surgical taxonomy.</span> Sunburst visualization of hierarchical classification from specialties (inner ring) to subjects (middle) and procedures (outer). Wedge size is proportional to procedure count.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.10555v1/surgical_non_surgical_examples.png" id="S1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/103;" width="215" height="103" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Examples of clips that are labeled as <span id="S1.F4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">surgical</span> and <span id="S1.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-surgical</span>. </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/descriptive_non_descriptive_examples.svg" id="S1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/84;" width="215" height="84"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 5: </span>Examples of captions that are labeled as <span id="S1.F5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">descriptive</span> (left) and <span id="S1.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-descriptive</span> (right). </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/raw_enhanced_examples.svg" id="S1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/84;" width="215" height="84"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 6: </span>Examples raw and enhanced captions after the contextual enrichment stage</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.10555v1/wordcloud.png" id="S1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/146;" width="215" height="146" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 7: </span>Word cloud of SurgLaVi captions, highlighting frequent surgical vocabulary.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/prompt_hierarchical_segments.svg" id="S1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/202;" width="215" height="202"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 8: </span>Prompt used for hierarchical semantic segmentation of narrations into tasks, steps, and phases.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/caption_validity.svg" id="S1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/112;" width="215" height="112"></object>
