<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.2 </span>Pre-training Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt a CLIP-style dual-encoder with a ViT-B/16 vision backbone (ImageNet-initialized) and a BERT-base text encoder. Outputs (768-d each) are projected into a shared 256-d multimodal space. A TimeSformer block encodes temporal dynamics over 16 frames.
We optimize a video–text contrastive objective (InfoNCE) with AdamW (lr=<math id="S1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=(0.9,0.999)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=(0.9,0.999)</annotation></semantics></math>, wd=0.02), cosine decay over 50 epochs, and batch size 312. We train the final model on a single NVIDIA H200 GPU. We conducted ablations on 8 H100 GPUs with global batch size 480 for 20 epochs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3 </span>Linear Probing Details</h3>

<div id="S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate frozen visual features by concatenating the 768-d backbone embedding with its 256-d projection (1024-d total). We train linear classifiers with batch size 256 and 50 epochs. Hyperparameters were tuned with Weights &amp; Biases <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> on single-frame inference for our model and each baseline to ensure fairness, then final probes used 32-frame windows with mean embeddings of the window representing the center frame.
The hyperparameter search spanned lr <math id="S1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{-3},10^{-4}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{-3},10^{-4}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, wd <math id="S1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,0.01\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,0.01\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and momentum <math id="S1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.9,0.95\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.9,0.95\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.4 </span>Temporal Probing Details</h3>

<div id="S1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We probe temporal transfer using an MS-TCN head trained on frozen frame-level features. Each batch is one full video. Across models/datasets, we use 3 stages, 8 layers per stage, and 64 feature maps. Optimization: AdamW, lr=0.01, wd=0.01, cosine schedule, 100 epochs. These settings are identical across models for fairness. Results are reported in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Temporal probing with MS-TCN ‣ 5 Experimental Validation ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.5 </span>Zero-shot Prompt Design</h3>

<div id="S1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#S1.F12" title="Fig. 12 ‣ 1.5 Zero-shot Prompt Design ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>–<a href="#S1.F19" title="Fig. 19 ‣ 1.5 Zero-shot Prompt Design ‣ 1 Supplementary Material ‣ SurgLaVi: Large-Scale Hierarchical Dataset for Surgical Vision-Language Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> show all prompts used for zero-shot classification in downstream benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10555v1/cholec80.svg" id="S1.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/79;" width="191" height="79"></object>
